validate -- validate a hypertext object
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        validate x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note markup list: Hypertext,, a hypertext object to validate
  * Outputs:
      * x, a *note markup list: Hypertext,, the input hypertext object,
        possibly with errors fixed
  * Consequences:
      * The hypertext is checked for validity, to ensure that the HTML code
        returned by html validate x is valid.

Description
===========

This function is somewhat provisional.  In particular, it is hard to check
everything, because our hypertext format includes some entities of class *note
IntermediateMarkUpType: IntermediateMarkUpType, that don't correspond directly
to HTML.  Either those will have to be eliminated, or a more-final type of
hypertext, convertible immediately to HTML, will have to be developed.

Ways to use validate:
=====================

  * "validate(Hypertext)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note validate: validate, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

