LATER -- a hypertext element for lazy evaluation
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        LATER {f}
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note LATER: LATER,

Description
===========

When the resulting hypertext element is processed later for conversion to html
or for printing, the function f will be evaluated (with no arguments) and the
hypertext it returns will be formatted.
+---------------------------------+
|i1 : f = () -> DIV { "hi there" }|
|                                 |
|o1 = f                           |
|                                 |
|o1 : FunctionClosure             |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : LATER {f}                   |
|                                 |
|o2 = hi there                    |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : peek oo                     |
|                                 |
|o3 = LATER{f}                    |
+---------------------------------+

