html(TEX) -- conversion of $\TeX$ to html
*****************************************

  * Function: *note html: (Macaulay2Doc)html,
  * Usage: 
        html t
  * Inputs:
      * t, an instance of the type *note TEX: TEX,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a string containing the result
        of converting t to html

Description
===========

This method produces an HTML string, mainly converting several simple text
formatting environments, such as bold face, italics, etc. Rendering
mathematical characters and equations is done by $\KaTeX$ (see
https://katex.org/ ), a JavaScript math typesetting library for browsers. See
the list of supported functions and symbols (see
https://katex.org/docs/supported.html ) for more information, or this page (see
https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/LaTeX/Mathematics ) for an introduction to math
mode in $\LaTeX$.

Equations in "$..$" or /// \(...\) /// appear in inline mode, such as $x^2-1$,
while those in "$$..$$" or /// \[...\] /// appear in display
mode:$$\left(\!\begin{array}{cc} x&z\\ y&w \end{array}\!\right).$$

In addition, {\bf ...}, {\em ...}, {\it ...}, {\tt ...}, and \url{...} are
converted to *note Hypertext: Hypertext, objects:

res(Module) is the method for making resolutions (see https://macaulay2.com).

Here are some examples designed to illustrate various other features of this
function when viewed in a browser:

+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\Gamma\Omega\pi$          |$\Gamma\Omega\pi$                             |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\partial\ell\infty$       |$\partial\ell\infty$                          |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\Re\Im\aleph\beth$        |$\Re\Im\aleph\beth$                           |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\NN\QQ\RR\CC\ZZ\PP$       |$\NN\QQ\RR\CC\ZZ\PP$                          |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\binom{n}{k}$             |$\binom{n}{k}$                                |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\sqrt[2]{\frac{a}{b}}$    |$\sqrt[2]{\frac{a}{b}}$                       |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\sum\prod\coprod$         |$\sum\prod\coprod$                            |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\bigoplus\bigotimes$      |$\bigoplus\bigotimes$                         |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
|$\bigcup\bigcap$           |$\bigcup\bigcap$                              |
+---------------------------+----------------------------------------------+
