Lastly, new macros can be defined using script tags. For instance, inserting
the following *note LITERAL: LITERAL, item in the documentation defines the
structure sheaf:

LITERAL ///<script> macros["\\OO"] = "\\mathcal{O}" </script>/// 

The macro can be used at any point after: $$ 0 \to 2\OO_{\PP^3}(-3) \to
3\OO_{\PP^3}(-2) \to \OO_{\PP^3} \to \OO_C \to 0 $$

