IntermediateMarkUpType -- the class of intermediate markup types
****************************************************************

Description
===========

An intermediate markup type is one that needs further processing to put it into
final form. A good example of one is *note TOH: TOH,, which represents a link
to a documentation node, together with the headline of that node, which may not
have been created yet at the time the *note TOH: TOH, link is encountered.
Another example is *note HREF: HREF,, which creates a link using the HTML <a>
element: when the link is created, the relative path to the target page depends
on the path to the page incorporating the link.

Protected objects of class IntermediateMarkUpType:
==================================================

  * *note ExampleItem: ExampleItem, -- a type of hypertext for holding example
    inputs awaiting outputs
  * *note HREF: HREF, -- hypertext link
  * INDENT (missing documentation)
  * *note LATER: LATER, -- a hypertext element for lazy evaluation
  * *note LITERAL: LITERAL, -- hypertext literal text
  * *note MENU: MENU, -- hypertext menu item
  * *note TEX: TEX, -- hypertext TEX item
  * *note TO: TO, -- hypertext documentation link
  * *note TO2: TO2, -- labeled hypertext documentation link
  * *note TOH: TOH, -- hypertext documentation link followed by a headline

For the programmer
==================

The object *note IntermediateMarkUpType: IntermediateMarkUpType, is a *note
type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note MarkUpType: MarkUpType,
< *note SelfInitializingType: (Macaulay2Doc)SelfInitializingType, < *note Type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type, < *note MutableHashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, <
*note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

